    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe refactor itself is structurally excellent \u2014 this is close to a model rename. The concerns are limited to one coherence slip.\n\n**What's good (for context):**\n- `OwnerCustomerCode` \u2192 `OwnerMemberId` stays the single authority for the identity format, and the Luhn check digit (previously `OwnerMapper.checkDigit`, a read-time derived field over `customerCode`) is correctly folded into it as the private `luhn(...)` helper next to `of()`/`regionOf()`. Logic now lives in the right unit.\n- The pipeline collapses cleanly from three steps (`AssignCustomerCode` \u2192 `DeduplicateCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignMembershipNumber`) to two (`AssignMemberId` \u2192 `DeduplicateMemberId`), with the fiscal-year segment absorbed into `OwnerMemberId.of()` via the shared `FiscalYear.yy`. No duplication, no step became a catch-all.\n- `regionOf` was appropriately re-implemented (leading-letter run instead of first-`-` split) to match the new separator-less format, and `withSuffix` collision handling still parses back correctly.\n- Rename is thorough: audit line/event, `OwnerCreatedEvent`, schema files, OpenAPI, and the cross-reference javadocs in `BusinessDay`/`FiscalYear`/`OwnerTelephone`/`AssignHousehold`/`CheckOwnerCityCapacity` were all updated consistently. No dangling `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` references remain in `src/main` (verified by grep).\n\n**Finding (actionable):**\n- `OwnerMapper.tenureFiscalYears` javadoc (`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java:179`) still reads \"so it matches the fiscal year **the membership number** and `fiscalYear` label use.\" The membership number no longer exists \u2014 this is a leftover reference to a removed concept. Every parallel doc site (`FiscalYear.java`, `BusinessDay.java`, the now-deleted `AssignMembershipNumber`) was updated to drop/replace that reference, so this one left behind is an inconsistency a maintainer would trip on. Update it to refer to the member id's fiscal-year segment (and the `fiscalYear` label), matching how the sibling javadocs were revised.\n\nThis is doc-only and small, but it's a concrete coherence defect relative to the rest of the change, so it's worth fixing before merge.",
